meta {
  name: Readiness
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/health/ready
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 when the dependencies needed to serve traffic are reachable, 503 when they are not.

  Two checks, weighted differently. PostgreSQL failing makes this Unhealthy, because the API
  genuinely cannot serve without it. Redis failing reports Degraded - still a 200 - because
  it is a cache in front of the source of truth: an instance that cannot reach it answers
  every endpoint correctly, only more slowly, and taking every replica out of the load
  balancer for that would be a strictly worse system.

  The body names which dependency is unhappy and nothing more. The exception detail goes to
  the log, where an operator reads it and an anonymous caller does not.
}
